  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-qc-tqc-periodic-square-cellulation": [
      "## Definition\n\nFix an integer $L\\ge3$ and write $\\mathbb Z_L=\\mathbb Z/L\\mathbb Z$. The\nperiodic square cellulation has vertices $q_{i,j}$, horizontal edges $h_{i,j}$\nfrom $q_{i,j}$ to $q_{i+1,j}$, vertical edges $v_{i,j}$ from $q_{i,j}$ to\n$q_{i,j+1}$, and faces $f_{i,j}$, for $i,j\\in\\mathbb Z_L$. Every index is\nread modulo $L$. The boundary of $f_{i,j}$ consists of\n$h_{i,j},v_{i+1,j},h_{i,j+1},v_{i,j}$. Equivalently, this is the quotient of\nthe unit square tiling of $\\mathbb R^2$ by translations in $L\\mathbb Z^2$.\n\nThe cellulation has $L^2$ vertices, $2L^2$ edges, and $L^2$ faces. The\ncondition $L\\ge3$ ensures that the four edges in each star and face are\ndistinct, and that every edge has two distinct endpoints and two distinct\nincident faces. The vertex-edge graph joins vertices joined by an edge. The\nface-adjacency graph joins faces sharing an edge; both graphs are connected."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-finite-square-cycle-is-boundary": [
      "## Statement\n\nIn the infinite square lattice, every finitely supported edge chain over\n$\\mathbb F_2$ whose incidence at each vertex is even is the boundary of a\nfinitely supported collection of square faces. The same conclusion holds for\nthe translated dual square lattice."
    ],
    "def-qc-tqc-toric-checks": [
      "## Definition\n\nFor the periodic cellulation in [[def-qc-tqc-periodic-square-cellulation]],\nput one qubit on each edge, ordered lexicographically by $(i,j)$ and then with\nhorizontal before vertical edges. The physical Hilbert space is\n$\\mathcal H_L=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes E}$, where $E$ is the edge set. For an\nedge $e$, write $X_e$ and $Z_e$ for the corresponding one-qubit Pauli acting\non that tensor factor and as the identity on every other factor. Define the\nstar and plaquette checks by\n\n$$A_{i,j}=X_{h_{i-1,j}}X_{h_{i,j}}X_{v_{i,j-1}}X_{v_{i,j}},\\qquad B_{i,j}=Z_{h_{i,j}}Z_{v_{i+1,j}}Z_{h_{i,j+1}}Z_{v_{i,j}}.$$\n\nAll indices are in $\\mathbb Z_L$."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-contractible-disk-lifts-to-plane": [
      "## Statement\n\nWrite the torus as $T_L=\\mathbb R^2/(L\\mathbb Z^2)$ with its periodic\nsquare cellulation. Let $D\\subset T_L$ be a nonempty compact embedded\ntopological disk with connected complement. Then the quotient map\n$\\pi:\\mathbb R^2\\to T_L$ has a lift $\\widetilde D\\subset\\mathbb R^2$ on\nwhich it is one-to-one and maps $\\widetilde D$ homeomorphically onto $D$.\nConsequently every finite primal or dual edge chain supported in $D$ lifts\nto a finite chain in the infinite square tiling, and cycles lift to cycles."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-toric-incidence-ranks": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor $L\\ge3$, the $L^2$ star-support vectors in $\\mathbb F_2^E$ have span\ndimension $L^2-1$, and their only relation is their total sum. The $L^2$\nface-boundary vectors have the same span dimension and their only relation\nis their total sum. The dual-face incidence statement has the same rank."
    ],
    "def-qc-tqc-toric-excitations": [
      "## Definition\n\nFor a nonzero vector $\\psi$ that is a simultaneous eigenvector of all toric\nchecks, its **e syndrome** is the set of vertices $q$ for which\n$A_q\\psi=-\\psi$, and its **m syndrome** is the set of faces $f$ for which\n$B_f\\psi=-\\psi$. A violated star is called an e defect and a violated\nplaquette is called an m defect. These are finite stabilizer-syndrome labels;\nthe names do not assume that a material contains localized physical\nquasiparticles.\n\nThe word **syndrome** follows the check-eigenvalue convention of\n[[def-qc-stabilizer-syndrome-and-logical-operators]].\n\nThe checks are Hermitian involutions, as verified below; thus their\neigenvalues on any nonzero simultaneous eigenvector are indeed signs."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-toric-check-commutation": [
      "## Statement\n\nAll star and plaquette checks of [[def-qc-tqc-toric-checks]] commute. The\nproduct of all stars is the identity, and the product of all plaquettes is\nthe identity."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-toric-cycle-quotient": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $Z_1$ be the space of primal edge chains with even incidence at every\nvertex, and let $B_1$ be the span of the face boundaries. Then $B_1\\subseteq\nZ_1$, the quotient $Z_1/B_1$ has dimension two, and the two winding\nparities give coordinates on that quotient. The same statement holds for\ndual edge chains, with dual vertex boundaries in place of face boundaries.\nThe horizontal loop $\\gamma_h=\\sum_i h_{i,0}$ has winding pair $(1,0)$,\nand the vertical loop $\\gamma_v=\\sum_j v_{0,j}$ has pair $(0,1)$; their dual\ncounterparts give the corresponding basis of the dual quotient.\nThe horizontal loop $\\gamma_h=\\sum_i h_{i,0}$ has winding pair $(1,0)$,\nand the vertical loop $\\gamma_v=\\sum_j v_{0,j}$ has pair $(0,1)$; their dual\ncounterparts give the corresponding basis of the dual quotient."
    ],
    "def-qc-tqc-toric-hamiltonian": [
      "## Definition\n\nFor $L\\ge3$ and couplings $J_e,J_m>0$, the finite toric-code Hamiltonian on\n$\\mathcal H_L$ is\n\n$$H_L=-J_e\\sum_{i,j\\in\\mathbb Z_L}A_{i,j}-J_m\\sum_{i,j\\in\\mathbb Z_L}B_{i,j}.$$\n\nThe energy unit is fixed by $J_e,J_m$. This is a finite-volume operator\ndefined from the stabilizer checks; its definition makes no claim about a\nmaterial realization or a thermodynamic phase."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-toric-joint-check-eigenspaces": [
      "## Statement\n\nDelete the star $A_{0,0}$ and plaquette $B_{0,0}$ from the full check list,\nand call the remaining $r=2L^2-2$ checks $g_1,\\ldots,g_r$. They are\nindependent commuting Hermitian involutions. For each sign string\n$s\\in\\mathbb F_2^r$, the operator\n\n$$P_s=\\prod_{a=1}^r\\frac{I+(-1)^{s_a}g_a}{2}$$\n\nis the orthogonal projection onto the corresponding joint eigenspace; the\n$P_s$ are pairwise orthogonal and sum to the identity. The omitted checks\nare determined by the retained ones, so every nonzero syndrome sector has\nan even number of e defects and an even number of m defects."
    ],
    "lem-qc-tqc-toric-string-syndrome": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $P$ be a primal edge trail with no repeated edge and distinct endpoints\n$q_0,q_1$. The Pauli string $Z(P)$ has commutation syndrome $1$ at exactly\nthe two endpoint stars and $0$ at every other star or plaquette. Let $Q$ be\na dual edge trail with no repeated edge and distinct endpoint faces\n$f_0,f_1$. The string $X(Q)$ has commutation syndrome $1$ at exactly those\ntwo endpoint plaquettes and $0$ at every other plaquette or star.\n\nIf either kind of edge-simple trail is closed, its corresponding string has\nzero syndrome at every check."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-code-dimension": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the periodic $L\\times L$ toric checks with $L\\ge3$, the common $+1$\neigenspace is a valid stabilizer code on $n=2L^2$ qubits. Its independent\ncheck rank is $r=2L^2-2$, so its dimension is\n$2^{n-r}=4=2^2$ and it encodes two logical qubits."
    ],
    "def-qc-tqc-toric-logical-loops": [
      "## Definition\n\nOn the periodic torus, define four Pauli representatives\n\n$$\\bar Z_1=\\prod_{i\\in\\mathbb Z_L}Z_{h_{i,0}},\\qquad \\bar Z_2=\\prod_{j\\in\\mathbb Z_L}Z_{v_{0,j}},\\qquad \\bar X_1=\\prod_{j\\in\\mathbb Z_L}X_{h_{0,j}},\\qquad \\bar X_2=\\prod_{i\\in\\mathbb Z_L}X_{v_{i,0}}.$$\n\nThe $\\bar Z$ supports are the two fixed fundamental primal cycles. The\n$\\bar X$ supports are the dual cycles crossing them. These operators are\ncalled the toric logical loops. As verified below, each is a nontrivial\nlogical Pauli class in the periodic toric code."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-gap": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the finite toric-code Hamiltonian\n$H_L=-J_e\\sum_q A_q-J_m\\sum_f B_f$ with $J_e,J_m>0$, the ground space is\nthe four-dimensional toric code space and the ground energy is\n$E_g=-L^2(J_e+J_m)$. The exact spectral gap above it is\n$\\Delta_L=4\\min(J_e,J_m)$."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-local-indistinguishability": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\mathcal C$ be the periodic toric code and let $\\Pi$ be its orthogonal\ncode projector. Let $D$ be a compact embedded disk in the torus with\nconnected complement. Let $S\\subseteq E_L$ be a set of edge qubits such that\n$D$ contains both the primal edge segment and its crossing dual edge segment\nfor every $e\\in S$. Then every operator $O$ supported on $S$ has scalar compression\nto the code:\n\n$$\\Pi O\\Pi=c(O)\\Pi$$\n\nfor some $c(O)\\in\\mathbb C$."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-mutual-sign": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $P$ be a primal path and $Q$ a dual path whose edge supports share\nexactly one physical qubit. Then their string Paulis anticommute:\n$Z(P)X(Q)=-X(Q)Z(P)$. This is the algebraic mutual e/m string sign."
    ],
    "def-qc-tqc-toric-energy-barrier": [
      "## Definition\n\nFix $L\\ge3$, $J_e,J_m>0$, a unit vector $\\psi$ in the toric code space, and\na specified nontrivial logical Pauli representative $Q$. An **elementary\nPauli path to $Q$** is a finite sequence $E_0,\\ldots,E_T$ with $E_0=I$,\n$E_T$ a scalar-phase multiple of $Q$, and\n$E_{r+1}=P_rE_r$, where each $P_r$ is $X$, $Y$, or $Z$ on a single edge and\nthe identity on every other edge.\n\nFor any prefix Pauli $E$, define its energy excess\n$\\varepsilon(E):=\\langle E\\psi,H_LE\\psi\\rangle-E_{\\rm code}$, where\n$E_{\\rm code}:=-L^2(J_e+J_m)$ is the energy of every code vector. The\n**Pauli-path energy barrier** of $Q$ is\n\n$$\\mathcal B_L(Q):=\\min_{(E_0,\\ldots,E_T)}\\max_{0\\le r\\le T}\\varepsilon(E_r),$$\n\nwhere the minimum ranges over elementary Pauli paths to $Q$. This is a\nfinite-code energy quantity; it is not a thermal lifetime."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-distance": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the periodic $L\\times L$ toric stabilizer code with $L\\ge3$, the\nminimum weight of a normalizer Pauli outside the scalar-phase stabilizer is\n$d(S)=L$."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-logical-algebra": [
      "## Statement\n\nThe representatives $\\bar Z_1,\\bar Z_2,\\bar X_1,\\bar X_2$ of\n[[def-qc-tqc-toric-logical-loops]] obey\n$\\bar Z_i\\bar X_j=(-1)^{\\delta_{ij}}\\bar X_j\\bar Z_i$ and commute within\neach Z pair and each X pair. Their four classes form a basis of the logical\nPauli quotient of the two-qubit toric code."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-constant-barrier": [
      "## Statement\n\nIf $J_e\\le J_m$, the horizontal logical string $\\bar Z_1$ has\n$\\mathcal B_L(\\bar Z_1)\\le4J_e$. If $J_m<J_e$, the dual horizontal logical\nstring $\\bar X_2$ has $\\mathcal B_L(\\bar X_2)\\le4J_m$. In either case a\nnoncontractible logical loop of the cheaper species has barrier at most\n$4\\min(J_e,J_m)$, independently of $L$."
    ],
    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-recovery": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $t\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}$ satisfy $2t<L$. Every finite Pauli error channel\nwhose Kraus operators lie in the span of Pauli operators of weight at most\n$t$ has an exact recovery on the periodic $L\\times L$ toric code. In\nparticular, every unknown Pauli error of weight at most $t$ is exactly\ncorrectable."
    ],
    "cex-qc-tqc-gap-not-physical-protection": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor each finite $L\\ge3$, the toric Hamiltonian has an exact positive gap,\ncontractible-disk local indistinguishability, and a constant upper bound on a\nlogical-string energy barrier. These unperturbed facts alone do not imply\nstability under arbitrary perturbations: the explicit global-projector\nperturbation $V_L=-\\Delta_L(I-\\Pi_L)$ closes the gap above the original\ncode space and enlarges the ground space, where $\\Pi_L$ is the ground\nprojector and $\\Delta_L=4\\min(J_e,J_m)$. This does not refute\nstability theorems for sufficiently small local perturbations, and it makes\nno claim about thermal dynamics or a material realization."
    ],
    "ex-qc-tqc-l3-toric-checks": [],
    "cex-qc-tqc-planar-is-not-toric": [
      "## Statement\n\nAt linear size three, the square planar surface code has asymmetric Z and X\ndistances $3$ and $4$, whereas the periodic $3\\times3$ toric code has\ndistance $3$ for both logical species and encodes two qubits. Thus the planar\nsurface-code calculation cannot be used as the periodic torus calculation."
    ]
  }
}
